tip: | Compare the head. | Seven rows of head on twenty-one rows of child: three heads tall. The Walker has a head nearly this big on a much longer body. Proportions say child, not size.
tip: 1 | Measure in heads. | Block the head, then stack two more of the same height, one for the body and one for the legs. Big head, no neck.
tip: 4 | Few details. | Two eyes low on the face and one pixel of blush. Moving the eyes down makes a face younger.
tip: | Try it. | Scale nothing. Erase two rows of leg and see how much younger it gets. | eraser
